<https://example.org/imaks/id/document/SOP-003> a im:Document ;
    im:documentText """[page 1]
Predictive & Corrective Maintenance Rules — Production
 Line A
Document: SOP-003 | Rev: 1.5 | Date: 2025-09-01 | Author: Ing. A. Conti — Maintenance Engineering
1. Predictive Maintenance Rules
Rule ID
Sens
or
Station
Trigger
Action
Priority
MAINT-01
VIB
ST04_PACKAGING
VIB DRIFT >0.05 mm/s
over 60 min
Inspect and lubricate
bearing
HIGH
MAINT-02
CUR
ST02_SEALING
CUR DRIFT >1.0 A for
30+ min
Inspect sealing jaw
HIGH
MAINT-03
TEN
ST03_LABELLING
TEN STUCK >10 samples
Replace sensor
MEDIUM
MAINT-04
PRS
ST01_FILLING
PRS <3.3 bar for >15 min
Inspect filter and pump
MEDIUM
MAINT-05
TMP
SRV01_SERVERRO
OM
TMP >25°C for >5 min
Activate secondary
cooling
CRITICAL
MAINT-06
TMP
WRH01_WAREHOU
SE
TMP DRIFT >2°C over 2 h
Inspect compressor;
notify QC
CRITICAL
MAINT-07
TMP
CHM01_CHEMICALS
TORAGE
TMP >20°C for >10 min
Emergency ventilation;
notify safety officer
CRITICAL
MAINT-08
HUM
RND01_RDLAB
HUM DRIFT >10%RH
over 60 min
Activate dehumidifier;
check HVAC drain
HIGH
2. Correlated Fault Resolution
Pattern
Primary Fault
Secondary Effect
Resolution
ST02_SEALING-CUR↑
→ ST04_PACKAGING-
SPD↓
Sealing motor
overload
Conveyor speed drop
via electrical coupling
1.Verify ST02-CUR trend. 2.Inspect sealing jaw.
3.Reset ST04 speed setpoint.
SRV01-TMP↑ →
SCADA latency↑
Server Room
overheating
Increased scan time →
apparent STUCK
readings
1.Reduce SRV01-TMP <25°C. 2.Verify PLC 
heartbeats. 3.Clear STUCK alarms.
WRH01-TMP↑ → QC
HOLD
Cold warehouse
drift
Product quality risk
1.Restore WRH01-TMP <8°C. 2.Notify QC. 
3.Place batch on HOLD in ERP.
""" ;
    im:identifier "SOP-003" ;
    im:pageCount "1"^^xsd:positiveInteger ;
    im:sourcePath "rules/SOP_003_MaintenanceRules.pdf" ;
    im:sourceSha256 "89bb8bebc3e0bc6ac9a157a9bc30b6de09fb526711cbc1c9631258444fe865b7" ;
    im:title "Predictive & Corrective Maintenance Rules — Production Line A" .

<https://example.org/imaks/id/document/SOP-004> a im:Document ;
    im:documentText """[page 1]
Personnel Zone Access and Alarm Response Procedures
Document: SOP-004 | Rev: 1.0 | Date: 2025-12-01 | Author: Ing. F. Ferrari — Safety & Compliance
1. Role-Zone Authorisation Matrix
Role
