2. Maximum Occupancy per Zone
Zone
Max Persons
Enforcement
Production Area
12
WARNING above 10; CRITICAL above 12
Server Room
2
CRITICAL above 2; access badge required
General Warehouse
4
WARNING above 3
Main Entrance
8
Monitoring only
Chemical Storage
4
CRITICAL above 4; hazmat training required — see RULE-CHM01-03
R&D; Lab
6
WARNING above 5; precision experiments may be disturbed
Cafeteria
20
Monitoring only — occupant comfort
3. Maximum Acknowledgment Times by Role and Severity
Role
Max Ack — WARNING (min)
Max Ack — CRITICAL (min)
operator
15
3
technician
10
2
supervisor
5
1
manager
15
5
security
20
5
4. Unauthorised Access Rules
RULE-ACCESS-01: Any entry by an unauthorised role MUST be logged as OccupancyEvent::UnauthorisedAccess
with person_id, zone, and timestamp.
RULE-ACCESS-02: Security personnel MUST be notified within 2 minutes of detection.
RULE-ACCESS-03: The KG node MUST include authorized=NO and a reference to this rule.

[page 2]
RULE-ACCESS-04: Chemical Storage has zero-tolerance policy. Any UNAUTHORIZED_ACCESS triggers
immediate escalation to the Safety Officer regardless of role.
""" ;
    im:identifier "SOP-004" ;
    im:pageCount "2"^^xsd:positiveInteger ;
    im:sourcePath "rules/SOP_004_PersonnelZoneAccess.pdf" ;
    im:sourceSha256 "925d9454d536f4510afb43cf58ca7646c6fd79676c65990bbaca233b56c763d9" ;
    im:title "Personnel Zone Access and Alarm Response Procedures" .

